  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -14,10 +14,14 @@ It is used for troubleshooting, analysis, development and education.\n \n == What’s New\n \n-NOTE: This is the last release branch that supports 32-bit Windows.\n-Updates will no longer be available after May 22, 2024 on that platform.\n+NOTE: This is the last release branch with support for 32-bit Windows.\n+Updates will no longer be available after May 22, 2024 for that platform.\n wsbuglink:17779[]\n \n+The Windows installers are now built with Visual Studio 2022.\n+\n+RPM packaging has been improved.\n+\n // The Windows installers now ship with Npcap 1.31.\n // They previously shipped with Npcap 1.10.\n \n@@ -48,6 +52,24 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark keeps banging out random chords on your piano and yelling “LIPS LIKE SUGUAR, SUGAR KISSES” because it was funny that one time at a party.\n \n+* Build failure with GCC 7.5, Linux wsbuglink:17911[].\n+\n+* RDP dissected as SSL wsbuglink:17952[].\n+\n+* IPFIX/cflow dissector asserts when varlen field length is zero wsbuglink:18010[].\n+\n+* 802.11ax HE PHY \"Device Class\" dissected incorrectly wsbuglink:18030[].\n+\n+* DHCPv6 Option 15 User-Class incorrectly parsed in Wireshark wsbuglink:18032[].\n+\n+* ICMPv6 dissector: PREF64 option parsing only works for prefix length 96 wsbuglink:18033[].\n+\n+* Switch macOS updater to Sparkle 2 wsbuglink:18035[].\n+\n+* CQL timestamp dissector displays the wrong timestamp wsbuglink:18038[].\n+\n+* Unable to dissect 802.11ax Target Wake Time (TWT) packets wsbuglink:18050[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n \n@@ -65,6 +87,14 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.4.9.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+CQL\n+DHCPv6\n+ICMPv6\n+IEEE 802.11\n+NetFlow/IPFIX\n+NAS-5GS\n+RDP\n+UDS\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
